    "source": "npm registry latest metadata; existing pinned versions retained"
  },
  "methodology": "Sequential fresh client workers with a separate fresh HTTP/SQLite server process per worker. Whole-client-process maxRSS excludes database server and coordinator. Each worker verifies output SHA-256, performs one warmup, then takes three timed samples (three requests/sample for 1/10/1000 rows; one request/sample for bulk). Natural GC, no forced collection. Time includes query construction, all HTTP requests including ExportLite cursor cleanup, protocol decode, JSON generation, UTF-8 encoding and completed drain to matching destinations. Imports, client/schema/Drizzle initialization and server startup are outside timing but client imports are included in RSS. Fixed 256-row batches and 64KiB buffering. No compression, disk output, TLS, bandwidth cap, jitter or packet loss. Fixed latency is added once to every HTTP request on the server, not per record or SQL batch. Protocol responses are written incrementally in 64KiB chunks for both cursor and ordinary pipeline requests. This JS fixture endpoint is not an actual Turso server; its response framing/serialization CPU can affect total time."
}
